      <p>Ireland is a full EU member state. Irish citizens benefit from Directive 2004/38/EC — the EU Citizens' Rights Directive — which gives EU nationals the right to move freely and reside in any EU member state, including Spain.</p>

      <p>What does this mean practically? You can pack your bags, travel to Spain with your Irish passport, enrol at a language school or university, and begin studying. No visa application, no consulate appointment in Dublin, no criminal record certificate required upfront.</p>

      <p>However, if you plan to stay for <strong>more than 3 months</strong> (which is the case for any serious study programme), you are required under Spanish law to <strong>register as an EU resident</strong>. This is simpler than a student visa process, but it is not optional — you should do it promptly after arrival.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── Short Courses vs Long-term Study ────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="msv__section msv__section--cream">
    <div class="msv__container--narrow">
