          <h3 style="margin-top: 0.75rem;">Under 90 Days</h3>
          <p style="font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--muted); margin: 0.5rem 0 1rem;">Short language courses, summer intensives, taster programmes</p>
          <ul style="margin: 0;">
            <li>No visa required</li>
            <li>No registration required</li>
            <li>Just your Irish passport</li>
            <li>Enrol and study freely</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div style="padding: 1.8rem 1.6rem; background: var(--white); border-radius: 14px; border: 2px solid #a0bfff; position: relative;">
          <div style="position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; right: 0; height: 4px; background: linear-gradient(90deg, #0066cc, #3399ff); border-radius: 14px 14px 0 0;"></div>
          <h3 style="margin-top: 0.75rem;">Over 90 Days</h3>
          <p style="font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--muted); margin: 0.5rem 0 1rem;">Full language courses, university semesters, degree programmes</p>
          <ul style="margin: 0;">
            <li>No student visa needed</li>
            <li>Must register as EU resident</li>
            <li>Obtain NIE number</li>
            <li>Get Certificado de Registro</li>
            <li>Register with local Padrón</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="msv__alert msv__alert--info">
        <div class="msv__alert-icon">ℹ</div>
        <p><strong>Key point:</strong> The EU registration process for Irish citizens is fundamentally different from — and much simpler than — the student visa process that non-EU nationals (like UK, US, Canadian, or Australian citizens) must go through. There is no visa application, no criminal record certificate sent to a consulate, and no waiting 30–60 days for a decision before you travel.</p>
